    "created_at": "2022-03-22T20:45:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-03-22T20:45:14Z",
    "body": "Sure! On this recoring I show a use-case when I want to delete the first label from a URL:\r\n* On the right in bash (same behavior with oh-my-zsh) I can jump between dashes and dots as well (on mac with option+left or right), so I can jump between i.e. any two labels in a DNS name and delete it (on mac with option+delete)\r\n* On the left with Starship, the same keys jump/delete only complete strings (whatever is between two spaces). Since I could jump only to the beginning of the URL I did not use option+delete key, but option+shift+delete which deletes stuff after the cursor.\r\n\r\nSo the jump action is more aggressive in case of Starship, which is I think less intuitive and effective.\r\n\r\nhttps://user-images.githubusercontent.com/311062/159571485-a2c7fdb8-e2f3-42a1-9e57-cd062aabf7e7.mov\r\n\r\n ",
