    "created_at": "2022-05-01T23:58:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-05-01T23:58:19Z",
    "body": "Sorry for the delay in responding, it's been a busy time here :(\r\n\r\nI did some poking around in this, and it seems that this is related to how readline decides what a \"word\" is in zsh. It seems that zsh has different defaults, and that omzsh overrides those to provide a better experience.\r\n\r\nYou should be able set the flag yourself by running the following code in zsh:\r\n\r\n```\r\nautoload -U select-word-style\r\nselect-word-style bash\r\n```\r\n\r\nCould you try this and let me know if it works for you?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
